# Тур 3

? Steven Johnson writes that in mid-19th century London, THIS was achieved thanks to hundreds of thousands of people. They were divided into something like castes: tinkers, dusters, ragwomen and others. Today THIS often starts within the household. What is THIS?
! waste separation.
= waste sorting, waste segregation.
/ In the mid-19th century, London already was a huge metropolis with more than 2 million people. But there was no advanced system for waste collection and recycling, so the city had to make do. The numerous waste collectors were split into many specialized jobs: For example, tinkers collected copper waste and positioned themselves much higher than, say, night soilers who cleaned out cesspits.
^ 
- Стивен Джонсон Карта призраков. Как самая страшная эпидемия холеры в викторианском Лондоне изменила науку, города и современный мир // http://flibusta.is/b/589970/read
- https://ecowiki.ru/marathons/recycle-waste/
@ Alexander Rozhdestvin

? As part of celebration of its anniversary, the Betis football club launched the sales of THESE. Having used one of THESE, one might see an element of the club jersey. What are THESE?
! pregnancy tests.
/ The offer is a novel way to greet new generations of players and fans. The two stripes for a positive test are green, to match the club jersey.
^ https://www.marca.com/futbol/betis/2023/09/12/65006ca922601d35508b4594.html
@ Vladimir Sushkov

? Film director Werner Herzog grew up in a poor family. To save on shoes and drawers, he used a certain rule. This rule is more often used to determine when it is alright… to do what?
! eat oysters.
= cook oysters, consume oysters etc.
/ Herzog recalls that shoes were worn only when they were absolutely essential — in autumn and winter. While in months without an R in their name — May, June, July, August — people went barefoot. This rule is more familiar when it concerns oysters, which are generally not consumed in months without an R.
^ 
- Вернер Херцог. «Каждый за себя, а Бог против всех. Мемуары» // http://flibusta.is/b/743770/read
- https://nplus1.ru/news/2019/11/21/oysters
@ Vladimir Sushkov

? During the Cultural Revolution, Mao Zedong’s speeches were recited at gatherings nearly every day. A modern book compares these directives to THESE. Identify THESE using only two words that begin with the same letter.
! Trump[’s] tweets.
/ Like Trump, Mao wanted to share his thoughts with everyone on a daily basis. But in the mid-20th century, the media were less technological. Mao’s directives were recorded verbatim via telephone and then read aloud at evening gatherings. по телефону, а позже зачитывали на вечерних собраниях.
^ Ай Вэйвэй. «1000 лет радостей и печалей» // http://flibusta.is/b/735231/read
@ Vladimir Sushkov

? Christian Dior used to begin work on his new collections in Paris, and then moved to the countryside where his ideas took their final shape. He compared these yearly trips to… what?
! spawning [run].
= breeding [run], spawn [run].
/ The French couturier compared his trips where the new collections were born to fish spawning runs.
