? In a film by Werner Herzog, a giant steamship is hauled across a mountain pass which separates two river basins. During the production, Herzog was reading a book about a certain person bearing THIS name. Robert Maudsley, who spent 40 years in solitary confinement, got a nickname referring to another person known by THIS name. What is THIS name?
! Hannibal.
/ To film the scene with a giant steamship hauled across dry land, Herzog was inspired by the works of Livy, who described Hannibal crossing the Alps with his elephants. Criminal Robert Maudsley got a nickname after Hannibal Lecter, who features in a series of books and films.
^ 
- Вернер Херцог. «Каждый за себя, а Бог против всех. Мемуары» // http://flibusta.is/b/743770/read
